# CADDY_TLS_MODE=local: Caddy sits behind a proxy that terminates TLS (Nginx
# Proxy Manager, Traefik, a cloud load balancer), so Let's Encrypt can never
# reach it to validate a certificate. Every site — the domain, its www/
# bookings/dashboard redirect hosts and the meeting host — is issued a
# certificate from Caddy's internal CA instead, and the proxy is configured to
# accept a certificate that is not publicly trusted (Nginx Proxy Manager:
# forward scheme https, port 443, "Ignore Invalid SSL" on). The browser only
# ever sees the proxy's own certificate.
local_certs
